> That one did indeed make to to the mine town---at clvl 2 due to
>a few accidental kills---until it got killed because of bad luck. I'd
>try it again, but I don't like the idea of being forced to play a
>particular race/class combination. I'd like to try a human samurai.

You'll have to play it carefully. The basic idea is to try to limit
encounters to one monster at a time. It's hard to do in the mines
because of the open space. You have to find some restricted passage of
the mine and camp out there with your pet. Monsters are drawn to you
but a large pet can dispatch easily.

The other tact is to use engraving to buy yourself some temporary
protection. Since you don't need to attack anything, an engraving
can last long enough for the pet to dispatch threats.

